  "id": "COMPOUND:26933 - PROTEIN:5867",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential relationship between 2-Methoxyjuglone and HaCaT through a series of molecular interactions involving enzymes and pathways. The drug appears to target multiple enzymes in the dehydrogenase/reductase SDR family, Lysine-specific demethylase 4D-like, and 26S proteasome non-ATPase regulatory subunit 14, all of which are involved in the metabolism and regulation of 5alpha,6alpha-Epoxy(22e,24r)-ergosta-8(14),22-dien-3beta,7alpha-diol. This compound, in turn, is shown to have a target on HaCaT, the human keratinocytes, indicating a possible role in cellular processes or signaling pathways. The integration of these pathways suggests that 2-Methoxyjuglone may exert its effects through the modulation of these enzymes, leading to a downstream impact on HaCaT cells. The evidence is consistent across different targets, highlighting a potential mechanism involving enzyme inhibition or regulation, which could be relevant to the biological activity of the compound.",
